From: bbzorba <bbzorba@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mp-frdm: limit Wi-Fi SDIO (usdhc1) to 100 MHz

The IW612 on usdhc1 intermittently fails at SDR104/200 MHz on this board
(cmd53 write timeouts right after NetworkManager starts, Wi-Fi dead until
reboot). Capping the bus at 100 MHz fixed it in all test boots.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific workaround]
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mp-frdm.dts	2026-11-16 01:11:42.411011636 +0100
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mp-frdm.dts	2026-11-16 01:11:42.411872778 +0100
@@ -969,6 +969,13 @@
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&usdhc1_pwrseq>;
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_usdhc1_vmmc>;
 	bus-width = <4>;
+	/*
+	 * IW612 Wi-Fi: 200 MHz (SDR104) is not reliable on this board: in about half of the
+	 * boots the first SDIO transfer after NetworkManager starts times out
+	 * ("cmd53 write error=-110") and Wi-Fi stays dead until the next boot.
+	 * At 100 MHz it worked in every test boot, still far above Wi-Fi 6 needs.
+	 */
+	max-frequency = <100000000>;
 	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	non-removable;
 	wakeup-source;
